---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Does the ₹5,00,000 DICGC insurance limit apply per account, per branch, or per bank?",
    a: "Under Section 16 of the DICGC Act, 1961, the ₹5 Lakh statutory limit applies **per depositor per bank in the same right and capacity**. All accounts (Savings, Fixed Deposits, Current Accounts, Recurring Deposits, and Flexi-Sweep FDs) across all branches of that same bank nationwide are aggregated into a single claim. Having accounts in 10 different branches of HDFC Bank does not increase your insurance cover."
  },
  {
    q: "Is accrued interest covered under the ₹5 Lakh DICGC limit, or only the principal amount?",
    a: "The ₹5 Lakh ceiling covers **both principal and accrued interest combined**. If your principal is ₹4,80,000 and accrued interest up to the date of bank resolution is ₹35,000 (total ₹5,15,000), DICGC will pay exactly ₹5,00,000. The remaining ₹15,000 becomes an unsecured creditor claim in liquidation."
  },
  {
    q: "How does the 'Same Right and Capacity' doctrine allow more than ₹5 Lakhs of insurance in one bank?",
    a: "If funds are held in legally distinct capacities, each capacity qualifies for an independent ₹5 Lakh cover within the same bank. For example, an account held in your sole individual capacity is separate from a joint account where you are the first holder, which is in turn separate from a joint account where your spouse is the first holder, which is separate from an account where you act as a guardian for a minor child, or as a trustee of a registered trust."
  },
  {
    q: "Why is a sole proprietorship account aggregated with personal savings?",
    a: "Under Indian commercial and tax law, a sole proprietorship is not a distinct legal entity or corporate person. It is simply a business name under which an individual operates. Consequently, under DICGC rules, funds in a proprietorship current account are legally held in the same right and capacity as the proprietor's personal savings, and are aggregated together."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the 90-day interim payout rule under Section 18A?",
    a: "Inserted by the DICGC (Amendment) Act, 2021, Section 18A mandates that if the RBI imposes withdrawal caps or a moratorium on a bank, depositors do not have to wait years for liquidation. The bank must submit depositor lists within 45 days, DICGC verifies within 30 days, and funds up to ₹5 Lakhs are disbursed directly to depositors within 15 days, guaranteeing relief within 90 days."
  },
  {
    q: "Which banks in India are categorized as Domestic Systemically Important Banks (D-SIBs)?",
    a: "The Reserve Bank of India designates State Bank of India (SBI), HDFC Bank, and ICICI Bank as D-SIBs ('Too Big to Fail'). These institutions must hold higher Common Equity Tier 1 (CET1) capital surcharges: SBI holds an extra 0.80%, HDFC Bank holds an extra 0.40%, and ICICI Bank holds an extra 0.20%."
  },
  {
    q: "Does auto-sweep qualify for the Section 80TTA income tax exemption?",
    a: "No. Section 80TTA explicitly restricts the ₹10,000 tax deduction to interest earned on *savings bank accounts*. The portion of interest earned on swept fixed deposits is classified as term deposit interest, which is fully taxable at your personal marginal income tax slab. Resident senior citizens (60+), however, can claim up to ₹50,000 across both savings and FD interest under Section 80TTB."
  },
  {
    q: "If I appoint a nominee on my bank account, do they become the legal owner of the money when I die?",
    a: "No. The Supreme Court of India (*Sarbati Devi v. Usha Devi*) has ruled that a nominee is merely a fiduciary trustee/bailee. The bank hands the money to the nominee to receive a legal discharge under Section 45ZA of the Banking Regulation Act, 1949. The nominee is legally obligated to hold and distribute those funds to the rightful legal heirs according to the deceased's will or succession law."
  },
  {
    q: "What should I do immediately if I notice an unauthorized UPI or net-banking debit?",
    a: "Under RBI Customer Protection guidelines, notify your bank in writing within **3 working days** to qualify for **Zero Customer Liability**. The bank is statutorily required to credit the funds back (shadow reversal) within 10 working days. Also call the National Cyber Crime Helpline **1930** immediately to freeze the beneficiary account."
  },
  {
    q: "What happens to a bank account that has had no transactions for 10 years?",
    a: "After 2 continuous years of no customer-induced activity, an account becomes 'Inoperative' (banks cannot levy minimum balance penalties). If it remains unclaimed for 10 continuous years, the principal and interest are transferred to the RBI Depositor Education and Awareness (DEA) Fund under Section 26A of the Banking Regulation Act. It can be searched and reclaimed via the RBI UDGAM portal (`udgam.rbi.org.in`)."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Frequently Asked Questions — Banking Risk & Deposit Systems"
  description="Authoritative answers to critical questions on DICGC insurance limits, joint account capacity rules, auto-sweep taxation, D-SIB systemic safety, and fraud liability."
>
  <div class="container container-narrow faq-page">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href={`${basePath}/`}>Home</a> &gt; 
      <span>FAQ</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="badge badge-gold">INSTITUTIONAL ANSWERS</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">
        Direct, statutory explanations resolving the most prevalent questions regarding Indian banking safety, deposit limits, and operational rules.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="faq-list">
      {faqs.map((item, idx) => (
        <details class="card faq-item" open={idx < 3}>
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">▾</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p set:html={item.a}></p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .faq-page {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--iq-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--iq-text-secondary);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--iq-border);
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--iq-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--iq-surface);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .faq-question {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--iq-text-primary);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-toggle {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--iq-rupee-gold);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  details[open] .faq-toggle {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--iq-border-subtle);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--iq-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
